\subsection{Training Configuration}
All experiments use the following configuration unless otherwise specified:
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Backbone}: Custom convolutional U-Net++ (approx. 9.1M parameters; alternative backbones like RETFound \cite{zhou2023foundation} are reserved for future work).
    \item \textbf{Loss Function}: $L_{total} = 1.0 \cdot L_{BCE} + 0.5 \cdot L_{Tversky}(\alpha=0.7,\beta=0.3) + 0.1 \cdot L_{Topo} + 0.3 \cdot L_{SkelDice}$. These coefficients were empirically chosen to balance pixel overlap with structural integrity: $L_{BCE}$ provides dense pixel supervision, $L_{Tversky}$ penalizes false negatives (vessel disconnections) more severely than false positives ($\alpha>\beta$), $L_{SkelDice}$ encourages centerline accuracy without overwhelming width estimation (0.3), and $L_{Topo}$ provides light global topological regularization (0.1) without destabilizing gradients.
    \item \textbf{Optimizer}: AdamW (lr=1e-4, weight\_decay=1e-5)
    \item \textbf{Batch Size}: 8 (effective 16 with gradient accumulation $\times$ 2)
    \item \textbf{Patch Size}: 128$\times$128, stride 64 (50\% overlap)
    \item \textbf{Epochs}: 60 with early stopping (patience=10)
    \item \textbf{Curriculum Stages}: 
        \begin{itemize}
            \item Stage 1 (epochs 1-20): vessel\_ratio $\geq$ 0.05 (vessel-rich patches)
            \item Stage 2 (epochs 21-40): vessel\_ratio $\geq$ 0.02 (moderate vessel density)
            \item Stage 3 (epochs 41-60): vessel\_ratio $\geq$ 0.001 (includes sparse vessels)
        \end{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Topological Loss Activation}: Epoch 21 (after curriculum Stage 1 warmup)
    \item \textbf{Mixed Precision}: FP16 for memory efficiency
\end{itemize}

